Notes and recommendations (concise)
- Start with **PECOS + XR-LINEAR** (Strong): it gives runnable code, XR-LINEAR training/prediction examples, and production-focused engineering patterns (ANN, trees, C++ inference). Use `pecos/xmc/xlinear` to prototype a sparse baseline quickly. Repo: `https://github.com/amzn/pecos` and its `xlinear` README: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amzn/pecos/mainline/pecos/xmc/xlinear/README.md  
- For candidate retrieval at scale prefer **HNSW** (hnswlib) for low-latency incremental updates, or **Faiss** (IVF+PQ + GPU) when you need very high throughput / quantization. Test both on a realistic label-prototype embedding size before committing.  
- Use partitioned label-tree papers (Parabel / FastXML / Label Disentanglement / PECOS' clustering) if you want sublinear routing with explicit hierarchical clusters. For dynamic label insertion, prefer prototype-insertion or local-node retrain strategies (PECOS patterns help).  
- If labels expand frequently with few examples, evaluate **PKI / incremental methods** and hybrid retrain vs. adapter strategies.  
- For evaluation, include propensity-scored metrics and hierarchical precision@k to measure long-tail behavior and correctness on deep leaves.

